	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Lists the Claude Code sessions that are waiting on you, longest
wait first, and goes to one. Nothing here holds logic: every script is a
call into ~/bin/claude-tab. Alfred runs scripts with /bin/zsh --no-rcs
and a fixed PATH that excludes ~/bin, which is why each uses the absolute
$HOME/bin/claude-tab.

  cn        list the waiting sessions, return goes to the chosen one

The hotkey trigger ships with no key assigned: set one in Alfred to run
`claude-tab next`, which goes to the longest-waiting session and posts a
notification saying where it went (a buried peer's tab may only come
forward, and the notification then says to pick the peer in the peer bar).
</string>
